#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ferryd: the Mac side of Ferry (run by launchd as com.anurag.ferry; use the `ferry` command).

The Ferry Android app connects here over Tailscale (port 47821 on this Mac's tailnet IP; token in
~/.config/ferry/token; only the phone's tailnet IP is accepted). Over that connection:
clipboard text and images both ways, files shared from the phone (saved to ~/Downloads and shown
with a ferry-peek thumbnail), and live screenshots, which `ferry shot` requests through the
control socket ~/.config/ferry/ctl.sock ("shot" or "status").

Fallback while the app is not connected: text clipboard over adb with scrcpy's server (video and
audio off; it runs as the adb shell user, which may read the clipboard in the background). The
phone is found via adb devices, mDNS, ~/.config/ferry/adb_addr, then a port scan of the phone's
tailnet IP (~/.config/ferry/phone_host), since the Wireless debugging port changes on every
toggle and mDNS doesn't cross the tailnet.

    ferryd              run in the foreground (what launchd runs)
    ferryd install      install + start the launchd agent
    ferryd uninstall    stop + remove it
    ferryd status       agent state and phone connection
    ferryd adb-connect  find the phone over adb (all the methods above); prints the serial
"""

import asyncio
import ctypes
import ctypes.util
import hashlib
